---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show a run's metadata: id, status, timestamps, launcher, and description.

Created, Started and Completed are in the local timezone.

Elapsed is wall-clock time spanning provisioning, setup, fuzzing, and teardown. Creator is the name of who launched the run (a user, a CI job or an agent). The run also has its user-defined attributes (`attrs.<name>` params at launch) under Attributes.

An incomplete run also has its failure moment (Failure Hash/VTime), to pass to `runs_logs`, and a failure reason when the run reports one.

Examples:
  runs_show {"run_id": "<run_id>"}
